1
00:04:26,086 --> 00:04:32,086
If you're going to bury the truth, make sure it stays buried.

2
00:08:52,173 --> 00:08:58,173
I Know What You Did Last Summer is a horror, thriller,
mystery film directed by Jim Gillespie.

3
00:13:18,260 --> 00:13:24,260
After an accident on a winding road, four teens make the fatal
mistake of dumping their victim's body into the sea.

4
00:17:44,347 --> 00:17:50,347
Exactly one year later, the deadly secret resurfaces as
they're stalked by a hook-handed figure.

5
00:22:10,434 --> 00:22:16,434
Julie James, played by Jennifer Love Hewitt.

6
00:26:36,521 --> 00:26:42,521
Ray Bronson, played by Freddie Prinze Jr..

7
00:31:02,608 --> 00:31:08,608
Helen Shivers, played by Sarah Michelle Gellar.

8
00:35:28,695 --> 00:35:34,695
Barry Cox, played by Ryan Phillippe.

9
00:39:54,782 --> 00:40:00,782
Elsa Shivers, played by Bridgette Wilson-Sampras.

10
00:44:20,869 --> 00:44:26,869
Max Neurick, played by Johnny Galecki.

11
00:48:46,956 --> 00:48:52,956
I Know What You Did Last Summer is a 1997 American slasher film starring Jennifer Love
Hewitt, Sarah Michelle Gellar, Ryan Phillippe, and Freddie Prinze Jr.

12
00:53:13,043 --> 00:53:19,043
as four teenage friends who are stalked by a hook-wielding killer one year after
covering up a car accident in which they supposedly killed a man.

13
00:57:39,130 --> 00:57:45,130
It was directed by Jim Gillespie and written by Kevin
Williamson, who adapted the 1973 novel.

14
01:02:05,217 --> 01:02:11,217
It is the first in the I Know What You Did Last Summer film series.

15
01:06:31,304 --> 01:06:37,304
Williamson was approached to adapt Lois Duncan's
source novel by producer Erik Feig.

16
01:10:57,391 --> 01:11:03,391
Where Scream, released the previous year, contained prominent elements of satire and self-referentiality, Williamson's script for I
Know What You Did Last Summer reworked the novel's central plot to resemble a straightforward 1980s-era slasher film.

17
01:15:23,478 --> 01:15:29,478
I Know What You Did Last Summer was released theatrically in the
United States on October 17, 1997 by Columbia Pictures.

18
01:19:49,565 --> 01:19:55,565
It received a mixed reception from critics and grossed
$125 million on a budget of $17 million.

19
01:24:15,652 --> 01:24:21,652
The film was parodied in Scary Movie (2000) and is frequently referenced in popular culture, as well
as being credited alongside Scream with revitalizing the slasher genre in the 1990s.

20
01:28:41,739 --> 01:28:47,739
The film was followed by three sequels – I Still Know What You Did Last Summer (1998), I'll Always Know What You
Did Last Summer (2006) and I Know What You Did Last Summer (2025) – and a 2021 television series.

21
01:33:07,826 --> 01:33:13,826
The film explores themes of high school, police, blackmail, fisherman, letter.

22
01:37:33,913 --> 01:37:39,913
The tone is mind_bending and dark and intense.
